@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Azure Repos";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Azure Repos provides unlimited, secure, cloud-hosted Git repositories for your code management and collaboration.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- What is Azure Repos -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is Azure Repos?</h2>
        <p>
            Azure Repos is a set of version control tools within Azure DevOps that help teams manage their code efficiently. It supports both Git and Team Foundation Version Control (TFVC), providing robust capabilities for collaborative software development.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-repos-overview.jpg" alt="Azure Repos Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Repos supports Git and TFVC for efficient version control.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Key Features -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Key Features of Azure Repos</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Unlimited Repositories:</strong> Host unlimited private and public repositories in the cloud.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Branching and Merging:</strong> Easily create branches, work independently, and merge changes without conflicts.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Pull Requests:</strong> Review code efficiently with built-in pull request workflows.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>CI/CD Integration:</strong> Seamlessly integrate with Azure Pipelines for automated builds and deployments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Code Search:</strong> Quickly find relevant code across repositories using powerful search features.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-repos-features.jpg" alt="Azure Repos Features" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Repos offers powerful collaboration tools for developers.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Setting Up Azure Repos -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Setting Up Azure Repos</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to create and manage your repository in Azure Repos:</p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Go to Azure DevOps and sign in.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to your Azure DevOps project.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on "Repos" in the left-hand menu.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click "New Repository" and choose Git or TFVC.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Initialize the repository and start committing your code.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-repos-setup.jpg" alt="Setting Up Azure Repos" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Setting up an Azure Repo is straightforward and quick.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for Using Azure Repos</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Branching Strategies:</strong> Implement GitFlow, Feature Branching, or Trunk-based Development.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Commit Frequently:</strong> Regular commits help in tracking changes effectively.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Write Meaningful Commit Messages:</strong> Provide clear and concise messages for future reference.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enforce Code Reviews:</strong> Ensure quality by requiring pull requests before merging.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Your Repository:</strong> Set up permissions and enforce security best practices.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-repos-best-practices.jpg" alt="Azure Repos Best Practices" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices enhances collaboration and security.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Azure Repos is an essential tool for managing code in a secure and efficient manner. It supports teams in achieving better collaboration, implementing version control best practices, and integrating with DevOps workflows seamlessly.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-repos-conclusion.jpg" alt="Azure Repos Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Repos is a powerful tool for modern development teams.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>